   "success": true,
   "error": null,
   "response_text": "Fixed it. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**The bug:** In `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` used a strict greater-than:\n\n```python\nif quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:   # wrong\n```\n\nWith `BULK_THRESHOLD = 10`, that meant 11+ units got the discount while exactly 10 fell through to `return 0.0` \u2014 precisely the reported symptom.\n\n**The fix:** off-by-one \u2192 inclusive comparison, matching the stated \"10 or more\" policy:\n\n```python\nif quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD:\n```\n\nNow `bulk_discount(10, 7.5) == 3.75` and `bulk_discount(11, 7.5) == 4.12`, while 9 units still yields 0.0. Only `invkit/pricing.py` changed \u2014 no test files touched, and the full suite (4 passed) stays green.\n\nDONE",
